[]{#sub.challenge label="sub.challenge"}

Our solution to the above problems brings a new challenge: namely, the new square matrix is actually a submatrix of a larger matrix $\mathbf J(x,q)$, one with block triangular form which is a fundamental solution to the linear $q$-difference equation satisfied by the descendants of the colored Jones polynomials [@GK:desc]. Already for the case of the $\mathbf{5}_2$ knot, one obtains a $6 \times 6$ matrix instead of the original $3 \times 3$ matrix $\mathbf J^\mathrm{red}(x,q)$, or of the completed $4 \times 4$ matrix.

